//? Title: Longest common substring
//? Subtitle: Actual common-suffix rows, selected occurrence identities and the original shared run
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A common substring is contiguous in both sequences. The common-suffix dynamic
program extends equal diagonals and resets mismatches to zero. We retain the
original GeeksforGeeks/GeeksQuiz example, expose actual producing rows and
first-maximizer positions, and distinguish its rolling working storage from an
optional complete trace.
)

\toc

> A tiny suffix extension and reset

Let D(i,j) be the length of the longest common suffix of the first i and j
elements. Boundary values are zero. If a[i−1]=b[j−1], D(i,j)=D(i−1,j−1)+1;
otherwise D(i,j)=0. Every common contiguous run ends at some such prefix pair,
so the maximum of these suffix lengths is the global longest common substring
length. Only a diagonal can extend a contiguous match: taking an up/left maximum
would instead solve a subsequence problem.

For a=[1,9,2] and b=[1,2], the longest shared substring has length one, despite
the shared subsequence[1,2] having length two. The actual first strict maximum
selects value1. The later equal-length value2 does not replace it. The tiny
diagram links actual real cell observations without implying they are adjacent
chronological writes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcsubstring_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lcsubstring_trace({1, 9, 2}, {1, 2});
    std::print("| actual prefix i | actual prefix j | actual equality | actual diagonal read | actual " "written suffix length | strict new best |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &c : t.cells)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", c.i, c.j, c.equal,
                   c.diagonal, c.value, c.new_best);
    auto &first = t.cells.front();
    auto &reset = t.cells[2];
    auto &last = t.cells.back();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("first", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first matching cell\nD({},{})={}", first.i,
                       first.j, first.value)).node("reset", {6, 0},
                                                   std::format(
                                                   "Actual later mismatch\nD({},{})={}",
                                                   reset.i, reset.j, reset.value)).node("tie", {12, 0}, std::format("Actual final equal-length tie\nD({},{})={}, replace {}", last.i, last.j, last.value, last.new_best)).edge("first", "reset").edge("reset", "tie");
    d.save_svg("build/lcsubstring_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual prefix i | actual prefix j | actual equality | actual diagonal read | actual written suffix length | strict new best |
| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 1 | 1 | true | 0 | 1 | true |
| 1 | 2 | false | 0 | 0 | false |
| 2 | 1 | false | 0 | 0 | false |
| 2 | 2 | false | 0 | 0 | false |
| 3 | 1 | false | 0 | 0 | false |
| 3 | 2 | true | 0 | 1 | false |
\image(figures/lcsubstring_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual common-suffix extension, reset and strict-maximum tie.)
\alttext(The tiny shared subsequence has length two but the actual contiguous optimum has length one; a later tie preserves the first occurrence.)

> Original shared byte run

Retain a=GeeksforGeeks and b=GeeksQuiz. The returned run is Geeks, and the
actual producer selects its first occurrence at index zero in each input. A
repeated occurrence in the first input does not displace that strict maximum.
Positions below come from the producing DP, not a separate find() that could
obscure tie identities.

The native byte conversion maps every input byte to an integer in0..255,
including embedded NULs. This is case-sensitive byte matching, not Unicode
codepoint or grapheme matching. The original ASCII fixture needs no external
dataset.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcsubstring_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto a =
        dm::algorithms::lcsubstring_bytes("GeeksforGeeks"), b =
        dm::algorithms::lcsubstring_bytes("GeeksQuiz");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lcsubstring_trace(a, b);
    auto &r = t.analysis;
    std::string run(r.sequence.begin(), r.sequence.end());
    std::print("Actual selected run {}; actual length {}; actual first start {}; actual second start {}; " "actual DP cells {}.\n\n| input | source index | byte | selected occurrence |\n| --- | ---: " "| --- | --- |\n",
               run, r.length, r.a_start, r.b_start, r.work.cells);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    for (int side = 0; side < 2; ++side) {
        auto &values = side == 0 ? a : b;
        auto start = side == 0 ? r.a_start : r.b_start;
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < values.size(); ++i) {
            bool selected = i >= start && i < start + r.length;
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", side, i, char(values[i]),
                       selected);
            p.text(i, 1 - side, std::string(1, char(values[i])),
                   selected ? dm::graphics::RGB{37, 99, 235}
                   : dm::graphics::RGB{100, 116, 139}, 18);
        }
    }
    p.size(1100, 450).x_limits(-1, 13).y_limits(-.5, 1.5).title(
        "Original byte strings: actual selected contiguous occurrences").x_label("original byte index").y_label("input0 at y=1; input1 at y=0").save_svg("build/lcsubstring_original.svg");
}
```
