> Work, capture and edge cases

Every nonboundary pair is compared once, so n*m actual comparisons split into
matching diagonal extensions and mismatch resets. Strict best updates occur only
when a longer suffix is found. Swapping inputs can change tie selection and the
second-input working-row length; the API deliberately preserves the original
input orientation. Empty inputs produce an empty selected run with both starts
zero; the initial zero row remains a real capture observation.

Complete size/count geometry is checked before allocation. A trace admits
n+m+(n+1)*(m+1)+n*m logical input elements, completed-row cells and actual cell
records before copying/evaluation. Default cap is one million; zero disables
only that optional cap. Fields, row headers, capacities, returned/runtime copies
and bytes are excluded. Complete trace storage is O(n*m+n+m), whereas ordinary
auxiliary rows are O(m). No wall-clock timing is inferred from these selected
work counts.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcsubstring_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| original first length | original second length | actual comparisons | actual matches | " "actual resets | actual returned length |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}) {
        std::vector<int> a(n, 1), b(n, 2);
        auto r = dm::algorithms::lcsubstring_analyze(a, b);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, n, r.work.cells,
                   r.work.matches, r.work.resets, r.length);
        x.push_back(n);
        y.push_back(r.work.cells);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual comparisons", {37, 99, 235}, 2).title(
        "Actual quadratic work even when no values match").x_label(
        "equal original input lengths").y_label("actual evaluated suffix cells").save_svg("build/lcsubstring_work.svg");
}
```
